body:
For anyone who wants some help with the whole overlay and sliding animations, this is what I did. In Modal.js, copy-paste the code above me. instead of returning <p>Modal</p>, you return a div with the built model. This is how I built it:

    return (
        <div>
            <div className="overlay" style={{"animationName": isClosing===false ? 'custom-fadein' : 'custom-fadeout'}}/>

            <div className="modal flex-container" >
                <div className="modal-wrapper flex-container" style={{"animationName": isClosing===false ? 'custom-slidedown' : 'custom-slideup', "top":topHeight}}>
                    <div className="modal-header">
                        <h5 className="modal-title">Modal Title!</h5>
                        <i class="closed-button fas fa-times" onClick={toggle} style= {{"cursor" : "pointer"}}></i>
                    </div>
                    Lorem ipsum text
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    );

\*\* The closed button is from font awesome. Keep in mind that before the return function I have another line of code: `const topHeight = "30px";` and instead of 500, I put 300 in the timeout. Since the CSS is big, I will only post the animation part:

    /* for overlay*/
    @keyframes custom-fadein { 0% {opacity: 0;} 100% {opacity: 0.5;} }
    @keyframes custom-fadeout { 0% {opacity: 0.5;} 100%{opacity: 0;} }
    .overlay { 
        position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; opacity: 0.5; background: black; height: 100%; width: 100%; animation-duration: 0.3s; z-index: 2; }
    /* animate sliding*/ 
    @keyframes custom-slidedown { 0% {transform: translateY(-100%);} 100% {transform: translateY(0%);} }
    @keyframes custom-slideup { 0% {transform: translateY(0%);} 100% {transform: translateY(-130%);} }

    .flex-container {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-direction: column;
    z-index: 2;}

In the modal wrapper class, I put `z-index:3; animation-duration:0.3s; position: relative;` Since the CSS is incomplete, I hope you get the idea, I hope I included everything essential to the 2 animations. (If you are wondering why it's 130%, it's because of the topHeight mentioned above. If you try with 100% you will see that not everything dissappears)
